### This provides key steps to map protein sequences using miniprot and extract landmarks using genome coordinates produced by miniprot
### This is a more conservative way to map BUSCO genes as it uses protein sequences instead of DNA sequences 
## install miniprot, follow steps on miniprot's Github (https://github.com/lh3/miniprot)

## STEP 1: miniprot mapping 
## create an .mp file 

miniprot -d genome.mp genome.fa

## use the .mp file and map BUSCO genes downloaded from Orthod DB (https://www.orthodb.org)

miniprot -t 6  genome.mp refseqs_ancestral.faa >  genome.paf

## remove the tags column (column 12 in .paf file which contain tags)

cut -f1-12 genome.paf > genome_notags.paf

## STEP 2: Compare and dotplot 

